findings.body:
`InsecureSkipVerify: true` is set for every `NewClient()` instance with no environment or config gate. Any network attacker can present an arbitrary certificate and MITM ledger HTTPS traffic (credentials, payloads, responses).

The staging self-signed cert note and TICKET-77 do not limit this to staging — production builds get the same client.

**Fix:** pin trust with the staging CA in `tls.Config.RootCAs`, or gate skip behind an explicit non-prod flag that defaults to verify-on and fails closed in production. Example shape:

```go
tr := http.DefaultTransport.(*http.Transport).Clone()
if cfg.AllowInsecureTLS { // staging-only, default false
    tr.TLSClientConfig = &tls.Config{InsecureSkipVerify: true, MinVersion: tls.VersionTLS12}
}
return &http.Client{Timeout: 10 * time.Second, Transport: tr}
```
